  "body": "Fork synced at v0.16.0 (process files at PROCESS_VERSION 9); upstream main merged into the branch.\n\n## What changed\nThe 28-tool starter catalog moves from a Rust table in `tools.rs` to `assets/tools/catalog.json`, a `camcraft-tools/1` library (the #300 envelope), embedded with `include_str!` like the posts. `catalog()` keeps its signature, names, order and values, so no call site or test changes. `camcraft-tools` reads it with a small strict reader (`catalog_asset.rs`: format/version/units/name/duplicate/unknown-key/`is_sane` checks, errors name the tool); a failing embedded asset is logged and yields an empty catalog, never a panic. Decision (layering, embed vs runtime read, rejected options): `docs/decisions/741-tool-catalog-json.md`. Type is `refactor`: user-visible behaviour is unchanged.\n\n## How tested\n- Before deleting the Rust table, a test compared the JSON catalog with it tool for tool (Debug-equal, all 28): identical. The permanent pins are below.\n- `camcraft-tools` (all, 38 pass): `the_shipped_asset_parses_and_every_tool_is_valid`, `the_json_catalog_keeps_the_old_tables_values` (order + per-kind values), `a_bad_catalog_is_a_named_error_not_a_panic`.\n- `camcraft-app` `--test tool_library` (6 pass) incl. new `the_shipped_catalog_asset_reads_the_same_through_the_library_reader` (app `parse_tool_library` agrees with `catalog()`); also `tool_gate`, `cutting_data`, `tool_list`, `mcp`, `scripting`, `drill_reach` pass; ui lib subset (tool_number, ball_corner, footer, fresh_op) passes.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\nFull `cargo xtask gate quick` / batch (the diff touches `Cargo.lock`, which falls back to batch) and the other ui suites; catalog values are unchanged and pinned, so I ran the catalog-touching ones. No snapshots or goldens changed. The optional user-override catalog folder is not done.\n\n## New dependency\n`serde` and `serde_json` added to `camcraft-tools` (both workspace deps already in `Cargo.lock`; no new crate). `Cargo.lock` gains 4 lines.\n\nChangelog: The starter tool catalog is now the data file assets/tools/catalog.json instead of a Rust table (#741, PR #TBD)\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #741\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
